    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003ePork shoulder is the cheapest cut that braises well, full stop.\u003c/strong\u003e Belly costs more per pound and most of what you pay for renders out into the pot as fat.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eKecap manis is one bottle that changes a lot of dinners.\u003c/strong\u003e If your store does not carry it, soy sauce simmered with brown sugar gets you close, which is the standard home workaround.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eDried chilies cost almost nothing and keep for a year.\u003c/strong\u003e A bag in the pantry replaces three different jarred chili products.",
